From 920bc8a24b5dfe4594fe23333a0e9073313e94d7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: GibaxLeGrand <48137851+GibaxLeGrand@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 00:49:18 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 50/51] Runner: a pause at a game frame waits for the race in
 the game's-menus lobby

With SRNP_LOBBY=2 the relay counts frames in the lobby too, so pause_at below
the lobby's length paused there (frame 60 stopped the lobby). The count used
by SRNP_PAUSE_JEU is now 0 until the lockstep from the start state, where
frames count from 1 again: a pause at frame 520 lands in the level's intro.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/runtime/srnp_relay.cpp | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/runtime/srnp_relay.cpp b/src/runtime/srnp_relay.cpp
index 8800ede..79d609b 100644
--- a/src/runtime/srnp_relay.cpp
+++ b/src/runtime/srnp_relay.cpp
@@ -1012,6 +1012,10 @@ void GameFrameHook(CPUState*)
 
 std::uint64_t RelayGameFrames()
 {
+  // The lobby through the game's menus counts frames before the race too: a pause (SRNP_PAUSE_JEU)
+  // waits for the lockstep from the start state, where frames count from 1 again.
+  if (LobbyVanilla() && s_vanilla.load() != Vanilla::Synced)
+    return 0;
   return s_game_frames.load(std::memory_order_relaxed);
 }
 
